// probe_npc.hml — acceptance probe for `src/sim/npc.hml` and for the villager
// half of `src/art/meshgen.hml`.  Run it FROM THE NIGHTSHADE REPO ROOT, both
// ways, and they must agree:
//
//     hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_npc.hml -o /tmp/pnpc && /tmp/pnpc
//     hemlock  tools/probe_npc.hml
//
// It exits 1 on any failure AND on an assertion-count mismatch.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHY THIS PROBE IMPORTS BOTH src/sim AND src/art
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The import wall forbids `src/sim/**` from seeing `src/art/**` and vice versa,
// so the villager's triangle ladder is written down TWICE — once in
// `npc.hml`'s NPC_TRIS_* (which is what the visible-set budget is computed
// from) and once in `meshgen.hml`'s `mg_register` calls (which is what is
// actually built).  Two copies of a number in two files that cannot see each
// other is a drift waiting to happen, and the only place in the repo that may
// look at both is a tool.  So section M does, and asserts them equal.
//
// It also means this probe can measure the SILHOUETTE (section N), which is the
// one requirement in the brief that is not negotiable: *"a villager the player
// cannot distinguish from a Husk at 20 m is a bug, not a saving"*.  Section N
// rasterizes both at the real 320x240 pixel scale and measures it.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IS ASSERTED WITH A LITERAL, AND WHY
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CLAUDE.md rule 5: enemy caps were once mutable with every probe green because
// every assertion was relative to the config value.  So the DESIGN ANCHORS are
// pinned to literals here and nothing else is: five named villagers, the
// 4 / 9 / 18 crowd, the 32 / 96 / 192 regard bands, the 8 / 1 / 300 visible
// caps, the 210/90/28 + 48/28/12 triangle ladders and the 12/28 + 10/22 switch
// distances.  Every one of those is a number a design document states, and a
// change to any of them should have to come and edit this file.

